    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d577">

                <pb facs="0489" n="373" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg373"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.51/381.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Blanchard to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 23.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-12-24">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 24, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Sir: Referring to my December 2, 10 a.m., and December 12, 11 p.m., I have the
                    honor to forward herewith copy of the note dated December 10 which this Legation
                    addressed to the Department of Foreign Relations in compliance with the cable
                    instructions of the Department of State of December 7, 5 p.m., with reference to
                    the refusal of the United States to regard as legal the proposed issue of paper
                    money, together with a copy and translation of the note verbale received in
                    reply thereto under date of December 15, 1914.</p>
                <p>I have, [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">A. Bailly-Blanchard</hi></signed>.</closer>



                <xi:include href="d577-a1.xml" xpointer="d577-a1"/>
